# Cross-Surface Routing Builder Authority

**Purpose:** Eliminate ambiguity about **who owns** each URL builder. WRS-URL-01 mandates no duplicated host logic in apps — this document classifies every builder by authority tier.

**Rule:** Cross-host URLs MUST use **Guest Surface Host (GSH)** or **tenant-kernel** primitives. App-local helpers are allowed only for **same-surface** or **redirect-only shims** documented below.

---

## 1. Authority tiers

| Tier | Owner | May emit cross-host URLs? |
| ---- | ----- | ------------------------- |
| **A — GSH** | `packages/guest-surface-host` | **Yes** — canonical |
| **B — Tenant kernel** | `packages/tenant-kernel` | **Yes** — dev/provision bases only |
| **C — Web redirect shim** | `apps/web` | **Redirect only** — no rendering |
| **D — Portal-local helper** | `apps/portal` | **Egress to marketing only** — thin wrapper |
| **E — Forbidden** | Any app inline host math | **No** — `guard-wrs-routing` blocks |

---

## 2. Builder registry

### 2.1 Guest Surface Host (Tier A)

| Builder | Purpose | Lifetime | Migration |
| ------- | ------- | -------- | --------- |
| `resolvePortalPublicBaseUrl(host)` | Portal base URL | Permanent | Stable |
| `resolvePortalRegistrationUrl(host, tourId)` | Marketing/web → portal register | Permanent | Stable |
| `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl(host)` | Cross-host member egress (PCMS-003) | **Deprecated Phase 3** | [builder-migration-contract.mdoc](./builder-migration-contract.mdoc) |
| `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host, moduleId?)` | Registry-aware member URL | **New Phase 3** | Primary after Phase 3 |
| `resolveMarketingPublicBaseUrl(host)` | Marketing base | Permanent | Stable |
| `resolveMarketingToursUrl(host, cursor?)` | Marketing catalog list | Permanent | Stable |
| `resolveMarketingTourDetailUrl(host, tourId)` | Marketing tour detail | Permanent | Stable |

**Authority:** WRS-URL-01 · package `guest-surface-host`  
**Owner:** Platform routing  
**CI:** `guard-wrs-routing` (no direct tenant-kernel calls from apps)

### 2.2 Tenant kernel (Tier B)

| Builder | Purpose | Lifetime | Migration |
| ------- | ------- | -------- | --------- |
| `buildDevPortalPublicBaseUrl(...)` | Dev portal base | Permanent | GSH wraps this |
| `buildDevMarketingPublicBaseUrl(...)` | Dev marketing base | Permanent | GSH wraps this |
| `buildClubSiteUrls(...)` | API provisioning | Permanent | Stable |

**Authority:** WRS §5 · `packages/tenant-kernel`  
**Owner:** Platform infra  
**Rule:** Apps MUST NOT call directly — use GSH.

### 2.3 Web redirect shims (Tier C)

| Builder | Location | Purpose | Lifetime | Migration |
| ------- | -------- | ------- | -------- | --------- |
| `resolvePortalRegistrationRedirectUrl(host, tourId)` | `apps/web/src/portal/resolve-portal-registration-redirect.ts` | 302 web `/catalog/{id}/register` → portal | Permanent shim | **Not** moving to GSH — redirect-only, web-owned |
| `resolveMarketingPublicUrl(...)` | `apps/web/src/marketing/resolve-marketing-public-url.ts` | Web `/catalog/*` → marketing | Permanent | Respects `MARKETING_CATALOG_REDIRECT` |

**Authority:** WRS addendum §5 — register family B  
**Owner:** `apps/web` operator/public shell  
**Not GSH because:** Redirect happens inside web app route handler; no cross-app rendering.

### 2.4 Portal-local helpers (Tier D)

| Builder | Location | Purpose | Lifetime | Migration |
| ------- | -------- | ------- | -------- | --------- |
| `resolveMarketingPublicBaseUrl(host)` (portal re-export) | `apps/portal/src/marketing/resolve-marketing-public-url.ts` | Portal `/` guest redirect → marketing | Permanent | Thin wrapper over GSH or shared helper — must not duplicate host math |

**Authority:** Portal guest egress only  
**Owner:** `apps/portal`  
**Rule:** Must delegate to GSH internally or import shared module tested by `guard-wrs-routing`.

---

## 3. Decision tree

```text
Need a URL?
├─ Same app, same host, relative path     → relative href OK (e.g. /tours/{id} on marketing)
├─ Cross-host or absolute                 → GSH (Tier A)
├─ Web catalog/register redirect only     → Tier C shim
├─ Portal guest home redirect             → Tier D (wraps GSH)
└─ Inline template `http://${club}.portal...` → FORBIDDEN
```

---

## 4. Workspace package rules

| Pattern | Verdict |
| ------- | ------- |
| `href="/me/registrations"` in registration flow | **Forbidden Phase 3+** — use injected GSH URL (DL-38) |
| `href="/catalog/.../register"` on portal host | OK on portal only |
| Absolute URL built in workspace | **Forbidden** — platform injects at render boundary |

---

